        "instruction": "Create a comparison proposal between the baseline (from D새비교) and the new product (from D새견적). \nBaseline: Product A (10 days), Product B (20 days).\nNew Product: Product A (30M KRW), Product B (40M KRW).\nConstraint: Do NOT evaluate or discuss price. Only compare lead times/specs if available. Since only lead time is in baseline and price is in new product, the comparison might be limited or I should present the new product's specs if any exist beyond price. If no other specs, state that only price is known for the new product, but since price is excluded, the comparison is effectively empty or requires clarification. \nHowever, usually 'proposal' implies a recommendation. Without technical specs for the new product, I can only list the known attributes. \nLet's structure the proposal as a comparison table.\nColumns: Attribute, Baseline (Old Criteria), New Product (Arrived).\nRow 1: Lead Time. Baseline: A=10d, B=20d. New: Unknown/Not Provided (Only Price provided).\nRow 2: Price. Baseline: N/A. New: A=30M, B=40M. (Exclude this row or mark as 'Excluded per instruction').\n\nActually, looking at the inputs, 'D새비교' has lead times. 'D새견적' has prices. There is no overlap in attribute type (time vs money). I cannot technically 'compare' them on the same axis unless I assume the user wants to see both side-by-side. I will present the data side-by-side, explicitly omitting price analysis/recommendation based on price."
